CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ reference member reads through: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ reference member aliases x: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ local lvalue-ref binding to member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ tuple head bound: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ tuple head aliases y: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.ref]/6 (member access naming a reference member is an lvalue of
the referenced type) and [over.best.ics.general]/2 (a candidate with no
implicit conversion sequence is non-viable, not a hard error).  Distilled
from std::_Head_base<I, T&&> / _Tuple_impl<I, T&&>, whose members were
dropped ("bad reference initializer" swallowed) leaving map/tuple piecewise
construction bodyless.  g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
